    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d795">

                <pb facs="0803" n="545" xml:id="pg545"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857/30</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 10, 1915, noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 11, 10.15 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2866. Your 2155, September 6[7], 6 p. m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d795-f1"/>
                    Delivered request for report on <hi rendition="#italic">Hesperian</hi> to
                        Von Jagow last night. He said that
                    he did not see what business it was of the United States unless American
                    citizens had lost their lives, and said unless American lives had been lost he
                    would give you no report. He intimated that the explosion was caused by a mine.
                    Probably that will be the German position.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
